{"summary":"Accept all five amendments. One fixes a clear documentation mismatch, and the other four identify real robustness and validity defects in the shrimp probe suite, especially around the thermal-suppression control and how reproductive outcomes are asserted.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-21a3dd5d","decision":"accept","rationale":"The doc comment is factually stale. The probe runs with `total_days = 60`, so describing it as ~50 days / 1,200 hours is inaccurate and should be corrected for maintainability and review clarity."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-aa20fab2","decision":"accept","rationale":"The current thermal fixture does not provide a healthy control baseline. Recent output shows the cool arm finishing in severe nitrite and molt-failure stress, which means temperature is not being isolated. The exact tuning change can vary, but the amendment correctly identifies a real confound that should be fixed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-bdcd6707","decision":"accept","rationale":"The probe text promises more egg dropping in the warm arm, but the test only records egg-drop counts and never asserts them; current runs pass with both counts at zero. Given that `egg_dropping()` is triggered by instability or temperature swings rather than steady high temperature alone, the scenario or mechanism needs adjustment before that behavior is meaningfully tested."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b317f92d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Counting 10-day windows that merely contain any berried female is not equivalent to counting complete berried-to-hatch cycles. With a 14-day egg duration, one clutch can span two windows and satisfy the current `>= 2` check without demonstrating two full cycles, so the assertion is too weak."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-d4d6dec5","decision":"accept","rationale":"This is a real test-validity problem. The fixture claims to isolate temperature, but it runs 60 days without chemistry guardrails and still passes when the cool control ends in a nitrite crash. Relative warm-vs-cool checks are not sufficient if the control arm itself is chemically unstable."}]}